/**
 * data/b3/sound-boxes.js — the K-318 `sound-boxes` grapheme bank ×11.
 * EN block hand-authored (2026-09-14, the K-318 build session); the ten
 * non-EN blocks are GENERATED by tools/apply-b3-locale.js from
 * i18n/.draft-b3-<loc>.json after tools/validate-b3-draft.js (never hand-edit
 * a non-EN block here). Contract: docs/worksheet-gen/b3-designs/K-318-sound-boxes.md §5.
 *
 * Per-locale block:
 *   mode                  'chunks' (de/nl/sv/no read the approved `chunks`
 *                         grapheme layer) | 'bank' (every other locale: the
 *                         per-word literal below is the ONLY segmentation)
 *   capitalBox1           de keeps the vocab capital in box 1 (displayWord)
 *   strictPool            da: 'policy_managed_absent' — K-1 items must carry
 *                         NO policy_managed key at all (never `false`; measured)
 *   mergeDoubles          sv/no panel ruling (katt = k,a,t,t today)
 *   remergeAcrossSyllable vocabKeys whose bank rows re-seat ONE approved
 *                         syllable seam because a multigraph straddles it
 *                         (en `rabbit` rab|bit -> r,a | bb,i,t). For those keys
 *                         the validator checks flat.join === word and
 *                         rows.length === count but NOT rows[s].join === split[s].
 *   exclude               vocabKeys the locale refuses even though the word is
 *                         approved (the reason is the comment beside the group)
 *   texBoundary           the banked keys whose bank rows may be DRAWN as a
 *                         syllable boundary (the Syllables and Sounds face prints
 *                         one arc per row): multi-syllable, 'TeX' in the approved
 *                         entry's sources_agreed, and NOT in remergeAcrossSyllable
 *                         (a re-seated seam is not the approved boundary). The
 *                         gate re-derives the set and fails in either direction
 *                         (a listed rule-only key, an omitted TeX-agreed key).
 *                         EN measured 2026-09-14: 24 of 182 rows (397/607 EN
 *                         multi-syllable approvals are rule-only), so the Tiers
 *                         face ships in EN for `around the house` only (pool 10).
 *   bank                  { vocabKey: [[graphemes of syllable 1], [syllable 2], ...] }
 *                         nested by the APPROVED split (approved-words-<loc>.json
 *                         `split`), one string per box; a string of >= 2 letters is a
 *                         multigraph -> the 1.5x "wide" box with the tie arc.
 *   dots                  hak-stippen over the boxes at d2 (nl true)
 *   exemplar              the theme the type renders when no theme is pinned
 *
 * EN conventions (one box = one sound, the Elkonin convention K-2 teachers use):
 *   consonant digraphs  sh ch th ck ng qu wh ph tch dge
 *   vowel teams         ee oo ea ai ay oa ou ow oi oy ie ei ey igh aw au
 *   r-controlled        ar or er ir ur
 *   doubled consonants  ll ss ff zz tt pp bb dd gg mm nn rr cc (one sound, one box)
 *   silent-e carrier    se ce (the mute e rides in the box of the consonant it
 *                       follows: horse = h,or,se; fence = f,e,n,ce) — allowed ONLY
 *                       after a vowel team / r-vowel / consonant, never as a
 *                       magic-e that lengthens a single vowel letter
 *   x                   one box (fox = f,o,x — one letter, K children hear one "sound")
 *   REFUSED             true magic-e words (kite, whale, plate, gate, vase ...), silent
 *                       letters (comb, lamb, calf, knife), soft-c/-g words (pencil,
 *                       garage, giraffe), irregular vowels (oven, glove, shoe, iron,
 *                       apron, penguin), and words too long for any face (> 8 boxes).
 * The gate (qa/verify-b3-sound-boxes.js) re-derives every row against the approved
 * file and this whitelist; a word absent here does not exist for the type.
 */
